<title>USA: Amati, IBM extend pact.</title>
<headline>Amati, IBM extend pact.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amati Communications Corp said Friday it has extended its contract with International Business Machines Corp for the development and manufacture of internetworking products.</p>
<p>Financial details were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Amati and IBM have had a long-standing development relationship. Amati (formerly ICOT Corp) and IBM signed their initial agreement in 1989. Since then, Amati has been involved in more than a dozen different technology development and product manufacturing projects for IBM's customer base.</p>
<p>The relationship with IBM has accounted for a significant portion of the company's revenues.</p>
<p>Amati's connectivity products include local area network gateways, client-based workstation software and network data communications interfaces.</p>
